so restate the getfqdn hypothesis (or drop it) and ensure the instrumented spans still discriminate the true 35s long pole.","cohort":["G6"],"criteria":["G6"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.035,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Plan Context: 'CPython ThreadingHTTPServer construction synchronously calls socket.getfqdn(host), which performs reverse DNS even for numeric 127.0.0.1, making a fixed macOS resolver timeout the leading dynamic hypothesis.'","src/rebar/llm/workflow/editor.py:516 constructs _LoopbackThreadingHTTPServer, not a stock server.","src/rebar/llm/workflow/editor_server.py:55-61: _LoopbackThreadingHTTPServer overrides server_bind to call socketserver.TCPServer.server_bind and set server_name from server_address[0] directly; docstring: 'keeps the literal bound host without reverse DNS.'","tests/unit/workflow/test_editor.py:218-237 test_server_starts_and_serves_without_reverse_dns asserts reverse_dns_calls == [], proving the loopback editor never invokes socket.getfqdn."],"finding":"The plan's leading hypothesis H1 is grounded on a false premise: the editor uses _LoopbackThreadingHTTPServer, which overrides server_bind to avoid socket.getfqdn entirely, so getfqdn is never called on the loopback path and cannot be the 35s long pole.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fcb01edcb6c2dc21a","impact":0.85,"is_primary":null,"location":"Context (getfqdn hypothesis) and Plan bullet 5 (H1 prediction)","norm_id":"n4597bf27d22a7f5c","priority":0.765,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["The organic macOS run is used as the discriminating experiment; the getfqdn span reads ~0s, so H1 can never be confirmed and the 35s remains unexplained despite the instrumentation landing.","Author anchors the fix on a getfqdn timeout that the code already defends against, wasting a Gerrit round trip."],"severity":"critical","suggested_fix":"Reframe the hypotheses acknowledging the getfqdn bypass: since the loopback server never calls getfqdn,